MemoryError: BindCraft 2 ran out of device memory in the Evoformer backward at 576 tokens.
  complex   563 residues, padded to 576 tokens (tt-bio buckets the token axis to 32)
  asked for 75.5 MB in one DRAM buffer (6.3 MB in each of 12 banks)
  free      149.7 MB of 12.885 GB, largest contiguous block 1.4 MB
This is fragmentation, not a full card: 149.7 MB is free, which would cover the 75.5 MB request if it were in one piece, but the largest contiguous block in a bank is 1.4 MB against the 6.3 MB that bank needs.
What to do: 576 tokens fits on a p150a with the card to itself (the largest axis measured to complete a gradient round is 576), so something else is holding this card. Interleaved trajectories are the usual cause: pass trajectories_per_card=1 to run BindCraft 2's own one-at-a-time loop. Otherwise 19 residues off the binder takes this fold to 544 tokens.
The allocator's own refusal follows.
